From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] libpdfium: do not export the statically linked libc++

libpdfium links libc++ statically and exported 699 std::__1 symbols (locale::use_facet, ctype<char>::id, basic_ostream sentry...). libandroid_runtime
lists libpdfium.so (NEEDED 77) before libc++.so (101), so its inline `os << "text"` (every LOG(INFO) <<) bound locale::id objects and use_facet to
pdfium's copy while the stream's locale came from libc++.so: use_facet returned the wrong facet (a collate<char> for ctype<char>) and the virtual
widen() jumped into libc++'s rodata, SEGV_ACCERR. docs/HIDL.md. Against external/pdfium aac15c2e18a7 (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -170,6 +170,10 @@ cc_library_shared {

     ldflags: [
         "-Wl,-icf=all",
+        // libpdfium links libc++ statically; its exported std::__1 copy would win the symbol lookup of libraries that list libpdfium before libc++ (apklayer: docs/HIDL.md)
+        "-Wl,--exclude-libs,libc++_static.a",
+        "-Wl,--exclude-libs,libc++abi.a",
+        "-Wl,--exclude-libs,libunwind.a",
     ],

     export_include_dirs: ["public"],
